{title: Clay}
{artist: Grace VanderWaal}
{album: Perfectly Imperfect}
{key: G}
{capo: 1}

{start_of_verse label="Intro"}
[G][Em][D][C][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
You see a [G]girl in the [Em]hallway
And then you whisper to your friend, [D]"who is she anyway?"[C] [D]
You [G]forgot what she looks like in like a [Em]day
But your [D]words don't hurt me, I will be [C]okay[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Cause you [G]don't [Em]hurt [D]me[C] [D]
I [G]won't [Em]mold [D]to[C]

Your [G]silly words, I won't live inside your [Em]world
Cause your [D]punches and your names
All your [C]jokes and stupid [D]games
They [G]don't work
[Em]They don't hurt
Watch them just go right [D]through me
Because they [C]mean nothing to [D]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Try to change my shape
But [Em]baby I'm not Clay
[D]Sorry not today
Cause [C]baby I'm [D]not
[G]Try to change my shape
But [Em]baby I'm not Clay
[D]Sorry not today
Cause [C]baby I'm not [D]Clay
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Your silly words
I won't live inside your world
Cause your punches and your names
All your [C]jokes and stupid [D]games
They [G]don't work
No, [Em]they don't hurt
Watch them just go right [D]through me
Because they [C]mean nothing to [D]me
I'm not [G]Clay
{end_of_verse}
